# VIS Mitsumi/Gryphon CD-ROM Driver ROM Map

This is a concise ROM map for the embedded VIS Mitsumi/Gryphon CD-ROM driver.

## Driver identity

```text
0xED067  cd.sys /m:18 /i:5 /t:5 /d:mscd001 /h
0xED0A7  Copyright (C) Mitsumi corporation 1989,1990,1991
0xF14A2  GRYPHON CD-ROM device driver - Version is 2(33) 29-Sep-92
```

## DOS device-driver header

Header begins at:

```text
0xED08D
```

Decoded fields:

```text
next pointer       FF FF FF FF
attributes         0xC800
strategy offset    0x098B
interrupt offset   0x0996
placeholder name   12345678
```

Approximate resolved entries:

```text
strategy entry     0xEDA18
interrupt entry    0xEDA23
```

## MSCDEX relationship

The VIS ROM MSCDEX layer scans DOS device headers looking for an `MSCD00`-style prefix.

The embedded driver command line uses:

```text
/d:mscd001
```

So the driver is expected to register as:

```text
MSCD001
```

MSCDEX sees it through the shared prefix:

```text
MSCD00
```

## Command-line options seen in ROM

Current embedded command line:

```text
cd.sys /m:18 /i:5 /t:5 /d:mscd001 /h
```

Working interpretation:

```text
/D  device name, patches DOS device-driver header name
/I  IRQ/vector selection; current ROM uses IRQ 5
/M  buffer/sector count; current ROM uses 18 decimal
/T  parsed but durable effect not fully confirmed
/H  probes INT 2Fh AX=4300/4310 host/hardware service
```

Additional parsed options:

```text
/P  accepted but no visible durable assignment in this ROM path
/U  door lock/unlock behavior
/A  alternate feature flag
/N  boolean path flag
```

## Important driver variables

```text
0x0061       command/data port candidate
0x0063       status/phase port candidate
0x0069-006B  start MSF BCD
0x006C-006E  secondary MSF / count fields
0x00C5       drive mode byte
0x00C6       interrupt/vector selector
0x00C7       PIC mask value
0x00C8       PIC EOI/vector value
0x00CB       buffer count
0x00CD       transfer count base
0x00ED/00EF  transfer progress counters
0x0101/0103  transfer-size limits
0x03C8       retry counter
```

## Important routines

```text
0xEDA18  strategy entry
0xEDA23  interrupt entry / dispatcher
0xEF656  request command 80h handler, primary read path
0xEF8C7  sends C0 M S F 00 00 01
0xF08AB  generalized C0 packet helper
0xF094C  status/data read helper
0xF070F  MSF conversion helper
0xF071E  BCD-like conversion helper
0xF0CD9  INIT handler
```

## Primary read packet

The clearest read packet:

```text
0xEF8C7-0xEF8EF

C0, [0069], [006A], [006B], 00, 00, 01
```

Meaning:

```text
0xC0  Mitsumi read command
0069  minute, BCD-ish
006A  second, BCD-ish
006B  frame, BCD-ish
00
00
01    sector count
```

Generalized helper:

```text
0xF08AB-0xF08DC

C0, [0069], [006A], [006B], [006C], [006D], [006E]
```

## Status/phase behavior

The driver polls the candidate status/phase port at `0x0063` and watches low-nibble phase values:

```text
0x0B
0x0D
```

Then it reads response/data from the candidate command/data port at `0x0061`.

Working status-bit labels from repeated ROM use:

```text
0x40  ready / command accepted style bit
0x20  media change / attention style bit
0x08  data/status phase branch bit
0x04  completion/data-ready branch bit
0x02  state/error branch bit
```

These names are software-derived working labels, not yet hardware-trace-confirmed.
